  "wiring_bug_disclosure": "the first canonical lambda-search (lam 2/4/8, D1 lam=1e6, D2 beta=4) ran with loss_point reading self.w_feat instead of self.w_feat_point and no point_loss_coef \u2014 a formatter re-wrap made two string patches fail SILENTLY, so every 'lambda' run was effectively lambda=1. Detected via the total invariance of per-dim receipts; fixed at model.py (w_feat_point + point_loss_coef now live, verified by monotone lambda response afterward). Those runs are retained below as lambda=1 replicates; the within-class/asymptote analysis previously reported was based on them and is WITHDRAWN."
